{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789319732,"nonce":"FKsmA+UEf//LCNm5uO2gw+9DvoQ=","title":"The interpreter cannot call a var-args closure over a native entry","message":"hlp_make_var_args accepts any closure, and a host makes one over a C\nentry to hand Haxe a function of another language (caribou's callbacks:\nthe entry sends the packed arguments through its bridge). The\ninterpreter's CallClosure handled the var-args sentinel by taking the\nwrapped closure's findex and calling it as a function of the program, so\na native entry, which has none, failed with \"varargs wrapped closure has\ninvalid findex\". The compiled tiers reach such a closure through\nhlp_call_method, which calls the entry with its bound value and the\narray, so only the interpreter differed.\n\nThe interpreter now calls a wrapped native the same way when the entry\nis not a stub sentinel and not a function of the program, and coerces\nthe dynamic result to the destination's kind. The host_module fixture\nhands Haxe such a function (Greeter.adder) and calls it in every mode.","files":null}]}